{"id": "EUVD-2021-34900", "enisaUuid": "27816885-7c90-31b3-bf66-66b3343b795e", "description": "OrbiTeam BSCW Server 5.x before 5.2.5 and 7.x before 7.4.4 contains an unauthenticated path traversal vulnerability in the style_name parameter of the theme operation. Attackers can send GET requests to /pub/bscw.cgi/<id>?op=theme with ../ sequences in style_name to read local files such as /etc/passwd. Exploitation evidence was first observed by the Shadowserver Foundation on 2023-10-22.", "datePublished": "2026-10-22T10:57:31", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-22T10:57:31", "baseScore": 8.7, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://web.archive.org/web/20260421125237/https://sec-consult.com/vulnerability-lab/advisory/multiple-vulnerabilities-in-bscw-server/", "https://packetstorm.news/files/id/165156/", "https://github.com/projectdiscovery/nuclei-templates/blob/main/http/vulnerabilities/other/orbiteam-bscw-server-lfi.yaml", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/orbiteam-bscw-server-5.2.5-7.4.4-path-traversal-via-bscw-cgi"], "aliases": ["GHSA-pvhv-hmm4-4xwh", "CVE-2021-48017"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "b5621f46-a721-34ed-bafc-ea4388a579d6", "product": {"name": "BSCW Server", "vendor": {"name": "OrbiTeam"}}, "product_version": "5.0.0 <5.2.5"}, {"id": "b58c4c49-f4e6-32c2-98ab-ea058987313b", "product": {"name": "BSCW Server", "vendor": {"name": "OrbiTeam"}}, "product_version": "7.0.0 <7.4.4"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "68a63e6d-039c-3660-a99b-83d0491b84c8", "vendor": {"name": "OrbiTeam"}}], "isExploited": false}